.TH ZERODDS-BENCH 1 "May 2026" "ZeroDDS 1.0.0-rc.1" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
zerodds-bench \- end-to-end latency and throughput benchmarking on the ZeroDDS DCPS pipeline
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B zerodds-bench latency
[\fB\-d\fR \fIDOMAIN\fR]
[\fB\-t\fR \fITOPIC\fR]
[\fB\-p\fR \fIPAYLOAD\fR]
[\fB\-\-duration\fR \fIDUR\fR]
.PP
.B zerodds-bench throughput
[\fB\-d\fR \fIDOMAIN\fR]
[\fB\-t\fR \fITOPIC\fR]
[\fB\-p\fR \fIPAYLOAD\fR]
[\fB\-\-duration\fR \fIDUR\fR]
.PP
.B zerodds-bench info
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B zerodds-bench
runs micro-benchmarks against the full ZeroDDS DCPS pipeline using a
single-process loopback (one writer and one reader on the same topic
inside the same runtime). The full XCDR2 encoding, HistoryCache, RTPS
2.5 wire protocol, and UDP transport are exercised — no external setup
is required.
.PP
The
.B latency
sub-command times round-trip per sample and reports min / p50 / p99 /
max in microseconds.
.PP
The
.B throughput
sub-command writes as fast as possible for
.B \-\-duration
and reports messages/s and MiB/s.
.PP
.B info
prints backend capabilities (transports, encodings, modes).
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-d ", " \-\-domain " " \fIID\fR
DDS Domain ID. Default: 0.
.TP
.BR \-t ", " \-\-topic " " \fINAME\fR
Topic name. Default: \fIzerodds/bench/loopback\fR.
.TP
.BR \-p ", " \-\-payload " " \fIN\fR
Payload size in bytes. Default: 64.
.TP
.BR \-\-duration " " \fIDUR\fR
Run duration: \fI5\fR, \fI30s\fR, \fI2m\fR, \fI1h\fR. Default: 5s.
.SH GLOBAL OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show help and exit.
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Print version and exit.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success.
.TP
.B 2
CLI parse error.
.TP
.B 3
DDS or I/O error.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR zerodds-record (1),
.BR zerodds-spy (1),
.BR zerodds-monitor (1)
